,481,220,17,15,15,20,2418,220,7379,400,77,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe function $f(x)$ satisfies\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\]for all real numbers $x.$  There exists an integer $n$ such that $f(n) = 6n - 2005.$  Find $n.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9b5dd2453e33d710694bea7aa506aba5107605ce80a548140b46970ff00f156c"},"seconds":29.576067209243774,"seed":1045145984338818539,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005. \\]\n\nWe are also given that there exists an integer \\( n \\) such that:\n\\[ f(n) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nLet's denote \\( f(n) \\) by \\( y \\). Then we have:\n\\[ y = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nNext, we apply the function \\( f \\) to both sides of the equation \\( f(n) = y \\):\n\\[ f(f(n)) = f(y). \\]\n\nUsing the given functional equation \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we substitute \\( x = n \\):\n\\[ f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nSince \\( f(f(n)) = f(y) \\), we equate the two expressions:\n\\[ f(y) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nRecall that \\( y = 6n - 2005 \\). Substitute \\( y \\) back into the equation:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nThis implies that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nGiven that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\), we set \\( n = 6n - 2005 \\) to find \\( n \\):\n\\[ n = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nSolving for \\( n \\), we subtract \\( n \\) from both sides:\n\\[ 0 = 5n - 2005. \\]\n\nAdd 2005 to both sides:\n\\[ 2005 = 5n. \\]\n\nDivide both sides by 5:\n\\[ n = 401. \\]\n\nThus, the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies the given conditions is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{401}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{401}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
